Thus we can assemble_transport_leg after activating nodes and locking availability.

Next we need transport_leg_loading_authorized via authorize_transport_leg_loading. Precondition: transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized. So we need origin_availability locked (we have after lock), and candidate_task_profile_linked for origin_availability (we need to attach task profile to origin_availability). Already done in preparation.

Thus after assembling leg, we can authorize loading.

Now we need loading_container_available (we have loading_container_alpha and beta; we will use one for shift_candidate_beta). It is currently available (init). We'll need to load container onto leg using load_container_onto_leg, which requires loading_container_available (true), candidate_prepared (for shift_candidate_beta), candidate_transport_leg_linked (we have), candidate_loading_container_linked (we have), transport_leg_assembled (true), transport_leg_loading_authorized (true), and not loading_container_loaded.

After loading, we get loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked, and loading_container becomes unavailable.

Now we need to stage schedule candidate: stage_schedule_candidate requires candidate_prepared (true), candidate_loading_container_linked (true), loading_container_loaded (true), loading_container_leg_linked (true), candidate_task_profile_linked (true), not origin_leg_loaded (we ensured false via assemble_transport_leg), and not candidate_staged_for_loading (true). So we can stage.

Now we need candidate_operator_linked and candidate_skill_certificate_linked for shift_candidate_beta. We'll assign operator and skill certificate earlier.

Now we also need to have dispatched shift_candidate_alpha, origin_availability_alpha, destination_availability_alpha.

